{{also|Fragen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|vrāgen}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|frāgēn}}, {{m|goh|frahen|frahēn/frāhēn}}, which is indirectly derived from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*fregnaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*preḱ-||to ask}}.<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Frage, fragen}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-fragen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}
* {{IPA|/ˈfʁaːɡən/|[ˈfʁaːɡŋ̩]|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːɡn̩|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|fra|gen|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{head|de|verb|third-person singular present|fragt|or|frägt|past tense|fragte|or|frug|past participle|gefragt}}

# to [[ask]]
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[wonder]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''frage''' mich, wer mir helfen kann.|I wonder who can help me.}}

====Usage notes====
* Generally, ''fragen'' has always been a weak verb.
* The strong forms of ''fragen'' are secondary and now obsolete in formal writing. They live on in dialects and colloquial varieties.

